Enhancement: Further reduce memory usage for directories with many entries

Backing up a directory that directly contains a very large number of entries
kept the directory's complete metadata in memory: several hundred megabytes for
a million entries.

For directories with 50000 or more entries, restic now writes this metadata to
a file in the temporary directory while the directory is backed up, instead of
holding it in memory. A directory of a million entries now peaks at 208 MB
instead of 1248 MB. If no temporary file can be created, restic falls back to
the previous behavior. The snapshots created are unchanged.

